    "timeLabel": "03:45 PM - 04:30 PM",
    "timeStart": "15:45",
    "timeEnd": "16:30",
    "title": "ML Kit reloaded: hands-on with on-device GenAI APIs",
    "track": "Salle 1",
    "type": "Conference",
    "lang": "fr",
    "speakers": [
      {
        "name": "Julien Salvi",
        "role": "Engineering Lead",
        "avatar": "https://cache.sessionize.com/image/dd30-400o400o2-4NcyaNMS4awH1Zr87u5Gve.png"
      }
    ],
    "description": "Google has been quietly embedding Gemini Nano into ML Kit, bringing generative AI capabilities straight to the device!\n\nIn this talk, we'll explore the new GenAI APIs of ML Kit powered by Gemini Nano, all running entirely on-device with no cloud round-trip, no latency and no data leaving the phone. Through live coding, we'll integrate several of these APIs into an existing Android codebase and see what they can actually do in practice. We'll also take an honest look at the current limitations, device compatibility and real-world performances to help you decide if and when to adopt them in your own apps.\n\nDiscover how ML Kit goes far beyond barcode scanning and text recognition 🚀"
